        "text": "EuroRollup shows how crypto trades and fund investments settle in euros."
      },
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "start": 5,
        "end": 13.481,
        "text": "Starting with a thousand demo euros, I buy two hundred euros of test ether. The receipt shows the five-cent charge."
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
        "start": 14,
        "end": 21.846,
        "text": "My fund order waits for its valuation. At ninety-six euros per unit, three hundred euros buys three and one eighth units."
      },
      {
        "id": "s3",
        "start": 22,
        "end": 30.84,
        "text": "Now I ask what happens if Friday's fund cutoff moves from four to three. The model turns my question into one proposed rule."
      },
      {
        "id": "s4",
        "start": 33,
        "end": 42.389,
        "text": "I confirm the change and replay two orders. The earlier one still settles Friday. The three-thirty order now waits until Monday."
      },
      {
        "id": "s5",
        "start": 44,
        "end": 54.787,
        "text": "That leaves three hundred extra euros reserved over the weekend. On Monday the later order receives three units. Both outcomes come with a reproducible record."
      },
      {
        "id": "s6",
        "start": 55,
        "end": 59.751,
        "text": "Open the project on GitHub and replay the experiment yourself."
